00:28:42.730 --> 00:29:09.460
<v Ira Glass>It's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass. Each week, of course, we choose a theme, bring you a variety of different kinds of stories on that theme. Today's program, We Didn't. Stories of what it is that we do when we're not doing all of the things that we think of as our actual lives. We've arrived at Act Three of our program. Act Three, Same Time Next Year. This is the story of a couple that did not fall in love, did not get together, did not form a future, and some other stuff that'll be clear as this story unfolds.
<v Ira Glass>这里是《美国生活》。我是艾拉·格拉斯。每周我们都会选择一个主题，带给你关于这个主题的各种故事。今天的节目是《我们没做》。关于我们不做那些被认为是真实生活的琐事时，我们都在做什么的故事。我们已经进入节目的第三幕。第三幕，《明年此时》。这是一个关于一对情侣没有坠入爱河，没有在一起，没有形成未来的故事，以及一些随着故事展开会变得清楚的事情。

00:29:09.460 --> 00:29:27.150
<v Ira Glass>It all begins simply enough when Amanda Marks is 13, going on 14, and she goes to Madison Square Garden to buy tickets to the Rolling Stones' Tattoo You tour in the early '80s. And she stands in line next to a cute 21-year-old for three hours. And they get to talking and talking some more.
<v Ira Glass>这一切始于阿曼达·马克斯（Amanda Marks）13岁快14岁时，她在80年代初去麦迪逊广场花园买滚石乐队“纹身你”（Tattoo You）巡演的门票。她在一个可爱的21岁男孩旁边排了三个小时的队。他们开始聊天，聊得投机。

00:29:27.150 --> 00:29:45.340
<v Amanda Marks>So we go and get our tickets. And the way they did the system was it was completely randomized. And so he was right behind me in line, or right in front of me, but I ended up getting much better seats than he did. So basically, we made this deal that we would go to the concert together, and sell his pair, and split the money.
<v Amanda Marks>我们去买了票。那个系统是完全随机分配的。他就在我前面排队，但我拿到的座位比他好得多。所以我们做了一个交易，我们一起去看演唱会，卖掉他的两张票，平分钱。

00:29:45.340 --> 00:29:49.080
<v Ira Glass>Do you remember what exactly was attracting you to him?
<v Ira Glass>你还记得是什么吸引了你吗？

00:29:49.080 --> 00:30:01.680
<v Amanda Marks>I was a teenage girl. And he was this really cute guy paying attention to me. What wouldn't have been attractive about him?
<v Amanda Marks>我是个十几岁的女孩。他是个很可爱的家伙，又关注我。还有什么比这更吸引人的呢？

00:30:01.680 --> 00:30:25.610
<v Amanda Marks>So it's raining. We share a cab uptown. I'm going back to school. I've taken the morning off. I'm trying to catch my English class. And we start kissing in the back of the taxi. And the rain's hammering down. And it's just-- it's like the movies. It just couldn't be more romantic. I'm feeling so grown up at this point, just thrilled.
<v Amanda Marks>当时在下雨。我们合乘一辆出租车去上城。我要回学校。我请了上午的假。我想赶去上英语课。我们在出租车后座开始接吻。大雨倾盆。这就像电影一样。简直不能更浪漫了。我当时觉得自己很成熟，非常兴奋。

00:30:25.610 --> 00:30:38.160
<v Amanda Marks>So I go back to school, and I'm all excited. And I tell my friends. And one of my friends gives me this look like, "He's how old? He does what? He's an out-of-work actor? Like, ew." And I was like, "No, no, he's really great."
<v Amanda Marks>我回到学校，非常激动。我告诉了朋友们。其中一个朋友用那种眼神看着我，仿佛在说：“他多大？他干什么的？失业演员？好恶心。”我说：“不，不，他真的很棒。”

00:30:38.160 --> 00:30:46.290
<v Ira Glass>I love how he's an out-of-work actor is a turnoff even if you're 13. Even if you're in junior high school, it just doesn't play.
<v Ira Glass>我喜欢这种即使你13岁也觉得“失业演员”很扫兴的感觉。即使你在读初中，这个身份也吃不开。

00:30:46.290 --> 00:30:51.610
<v Amanda Marks>Like, oh, yeah, out-of-work actor. Out of here.
<v Amanda Marks>就像，哦，是的，失业演员。滚开吧。

00:30:51.610 --> 00:30:53.490
<v Ira Glass>So your friends are skeptical.
<v Ira Glass>所以你的朋友们很怀疑。

00:30:53.490 --> 00:31:08.610
<v Amanda Marks>Yes. Yes, they are. And it was weird because I wouldn't go to his house. I didn't really want him coming to my house. So we'd meet in public places, have these long, intense, involved conversations.
<v Amanda Marks>是的。是的，他们很怀疑。奇怪的是我不想去他家。我也不想他来我家。所以我们在公共场合见面，进行那些漫长、激烈、投入的对话。

00:31:08.610 --> 00:31:10.480
<v Ira Glass>Instead of making out.
<v Ira Glass>代替了做爱。

